STEPS=[
 ['Choose an interval inside the real domain and evaluate both endpoints; continuity is a separate requirement.','(a) [1,2]: f(1)=e−3≈−0.281718, f(2)=e²−4≈3.389056.','(b) [1,2]: f(1)=cos1≈0.540302, f(2)=cos2−1≈−1.416147. Angles are radians.','(c) [3,4]: f(3)=ln3−2≈−0.901388, f(4)=ln4−1≈0.386294; both endpoints are positive inputs for ln.','(d) [3,4]: f(3)=2, f(4)=−1.','All four functions are continuous on their chosen intervals and have strict opposite endpoint signs, so each interval brackets at least one root. Many other valid brackets may also be chosen.'],
 ['Use cⱼ=(aⱼ+bⱼ)/2, evaluate f(cⱼ), and retain the half interval with opposite signs. Do not round intermediate values before updating the bracket.','(a) Midpoints 1.4,1.2,1.1,1.15 have residuals approximately +0.65519997,+0.12011692,−0.09583398,+0.00819291. Final bracket [1.1,1.15].','(b) Midpoints 1.2,1.4,1.3,1.25 have residuals +0.16235775,−0.23003286,−0.03250117,+0.06532236. Final bracket [1.25,1.3].','(c) Midpoints 3.6,3.8,3.7,3.65 have residuals −0.11906615,+0.13500107,+0.00833282,−0.05527283. Final bracket [3.65,3.7].','(d) Midpoints 3.6,3.4,3.5,3.55 have residuals −0.04,+0.56,+0.25,+0.1025. Final bracket [3.55,3.6].','Each original interval has width 0.8; after four updates each final width is 0.05, confirming the halving count. The last evaluated midpoint is the fourth requested iterate, not a further midpoint of the final bracket.'],
 ['Regula-falsi requires continuous f and strict opposite endpoint signs; the chord formula is c=a−(a−b)f(a)/(f(a)−f(b)).','(a) e^x−x>0 for every real x: its minimum at x=0 is 1. In particular both negative endpoints give positive values. There is no real root and no valid bracketing iteration for this printed problem.','(b) The endpoints 0.8,1.6 have opposite signs. The first chord iterate is c₀≈1.2701241483, residual +0.0260381483; retain [1.2701241483,1.6].','Second c₁≈1.2832329128, residual +0.0003836222; third c₂≈1.2834259276, residual +0.0000055129. Update the positive endpoint each time.','Fourth c₃≈1.2834287013, residual +0.0000000792; retain [1.2834287013,1.6]. The negative endpoint stays fixed, illustrating that regula-falsi does not halve bracket width.','(c) On [−2.4,−1.6], x²−10x+23 is positive at both endpoints and throughout the interval. The actual roots are 5±√2, both positive and outside the given interval, so the requested regula-falsi bracket is invalid.'],
 ['The function 1/(x−2) is never zero wherever defined. Its denominator is zero at x=2.','(a) On [3,7], f(3)=1 and f(7)=1/5 are both positive. There is no sign-changing bracket, so bisection must not start.','(b) On [1,7], f(1)=−1 and f(7)=1/5 have opposite signs, but the function is discontinuous at the interior pole x=2.','The intermediate value theorem cannot apply across that pole. An endpoint-sign test alone is insufficient.','Naive updates can shrink toward x=2, or encounter an undefined midpoint in other intervals; this would approximate a singularity rather than a root.','Therefore neither interval supplies a valid bisection root problem, despite the sign change in (b).'],
 ['Use xᵢ₊₁=xᵢ−f(xᵢ)/f′(xᵢ), indexing x₀ as the initial value and calculating three updates.','(a) f′=3x²: x₁≈1.6666666667, x₂≈1.4711111111, x₃≈1.4428120982.','(b) f′=cos x: x₁≈−0.5574077247, x₂≈0.0659364519, x₃≈−0.0000957219.','(c) f′=3x²+2: x₁=0.5, x₂≈0.4545454545, x₃≈0.4533983367.','(d) f′=cos x: x₁≈−4.1850398633, x₂≈−2.4678936745, x₃≈−3.2661862776. Sine angles are radians.','Every used derivative is nonzero. These are specifically the third iterates, not claims of exact roots or of a requested accuracy; the sine start in (d) makes large initial jumps.'],
 ['The source gives intervals but no unique starting point, so choose their midpoints: 0.5,−2.5,−2.5. Check that each equation is continuous there and brackets a root.','(a) Use f=x³+3x−1, f′=3x²+3. Iterates are 0.5→0.3333333333→0.3222222222→0.3221853550. The last two both round to 0.322.','(b) Use f=x³+2x²−x+1, f′=3x²+4x−1. Iterates −2.5→−2.5483870968→−2.5468199525→−2.5468182769. The last two round to −2.547.','(c) Use f=∛(x−3)−x−1 and f′=1/[3(∛(x−3))²]−1, retaining real cube roots. Iterates −2.5→−2.7969409897→−2.7963219058→−2.7963219033. The last two round to −2.796.','The final residuals are about 1.31×10^(−9), −1.58×10^(−11) and −4.44×10^(−16), respectively, independently checking substitution. Derivatives remain nonzero and iterates stay in the specified intervals.','Agreement of successive rounded iterates is the requested stopping rule, not a universal error proof. Here the residuals and nonzero derivatives near the simple roots support the displayed approximations.'],
 ['The source requests Maple fsolve with initial start 0.5; no output is printed on this exercise page.','Independently solve the quadratic using the formula: x=[−4±√(16+36)]/6.','Simplify to x=(−2±√13)/3.','The roots are approximately 0.5351837585 and −1.8685170918. The start 0.5 is near the positive root.','The intended nearby numerical solution is x≈0.5351837585; an unrestricted polynomial solve can report both roots.','These are exact-algebra and numerical checks of the requested result, not a claim that Maple was executed. Substitution of the exact expressions makes 3x²+4x−3 zero.']
]
