HISTORY=[heading('History'),figure('numerical316-qusta','Qusta Ibn Luqa (820–912)','Source portrait labelled Qusta Ibn Luqa.'),paragraph('Qusta Ibn Luqa was a Syrian mathematician, astronomer and philosopher. He contribute in many fields of science, medicine, astronomy. His translation on the difference between the spirit and the soul was one of the few works not attributed to Aristotle that was included in a list of books to be read or lectured on. He was the first person to write the double false position in 10th century. He justified the technique by a formal, Euclidean-style geometric proof, within the tradition of Muslim mathematics. Double false position was known as Hisab-al-Khata’ayn. It was used for centuries to solve practical problems such as commercial and recreational problems.'),note('The history passage is transcribed source material; historical dates and priority claims are not independently verified here. Modern regula-falsi and historical double false position should not be conflated just because both names include false position.')]
